{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 1 RCA — completion-validator incident reclassified; no recovery-code fix is yet justified.\n\nObserved ordering: the second 8322 completion verdict was emitted at event timestamp 1786063291486790001. It rejected Gerrit change 1455 / both +1 votes / run 31131797081 / mirror SHA 81b3b59294 as ticket-only evidence. The exact `[operator-attested]` tag was added afterward at 1786063328784010001 (37.30s later). ADR 0043 and `completion_verifier.md:81-86` deliberately classify every untagged criterion as codebase-verifiable, for which a ticket comment alone is insufficient. Therefore that recorded rejection was intended strict-tag behavior, not proof of a bounded-recovery defect.\n\nDiscriminating runtime probes used the production completion model `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` with temperature 0 and the current tagged 8322 material. Current gatherer -> current finalizer passed the concrete operator attestation 3/3, emitted `kind=operator-attested, met=true`, and cited the ticket provenance. The same pipeline with an experimental co-located gatherer rule also passed 3/3. A direct current-finalizer probe given the exact tagged criterion and concrete bounded evidence likewise passed 3/3. Thus provenance is neither omitted nor truncated in the current tagged path, and the finalizer does not reject it. These outcomes reject the planned recovery/finalizer RCA.\n\nThe genuine defect exposed by the incident is the remediation-contract mismatch at `src/rebar/llm/completion.py:48-65`: every FAIL says concrete ticket-comment evidence will be considered on retry, but it omits the exact `[operator-attested]` tag prerequisite for external evidence. The operator followed that guidance, added a concrete comment, and received the contractually correct second FAIL because the criterion was still untagged. This is multi-file contract drift relative to ADR 0043 / `completion_verifier.md:68-94`, not evidence-recovery loss.\n\nDefect legitimacy: the historical untagged verdict is intended behavior. The generic remediation wording is a defect because it directs callers to a retry that cannot satisfy an untagged external criterion. Per rebar-debug, no Phase-2 edit to `completion_recovery.py` or `completion_verifier_finalizer.md` is authorized by the evidence. Next: replicate `verify-completion 8322` with the exact tag, then either close/reclassify this ticket if the blocker is gone or re-scope it to the remediation wording under a fresh plan review."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786067545030457001,"uuid":"221acc70-5d2a-4e78-a3f5-96df7ee36475"}